{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"mutating"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"reserveCapacity"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"_"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"internalParam","text":"minimumCapacity"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Int","text":"Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"platforms":["macOS"]}]},{"kind":"parameters","parameters":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The requested number of elements to store."}]}],"name":"minimumCapacity"}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If you are adding a known number of elements to an array, use this method"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to avoid multiple reallocations. This method ensures that the array has"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"unique, mutable, contiguous storage, with space allocated for at least"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the requested number of elements."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Calling the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reserveCapacity(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" method on an array with bridged storage"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"triggers a copy to contiguous storage even if the existing storage"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"has room to store "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"minimumCapacity"},{"type":"text","text":" elements."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For performance reasons, the size of the newly allocated storage might be"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"greater than the requested capacity. Use the array’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"capacity"},{"type":"text","text":" property"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to determine the size of the new storage."}]},{"text":"Preserving an Array’s Geometric Growth Strategy","anchor":"Preserving-an-Arrays-Geometric-Growth-Strategy","type":"heading","level":1},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If you implement a custom data structure backed by an array that grows"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"dynamically, naively calling the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reserveCapacity(_:)"},{"text":" method can lead","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to worse than expected performance. Arrays need to follow a geometric"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"allocation pattern for appending elements to achieve amortized","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"constant-time performance. The ","type":"text"},{"code":"Array","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" type’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"append(_:)"},{"text":" and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"append(contentsOf:)"},{"type":"text","text":" methods take care of this detail for you, but"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reserveCapacity(_:)"},{"text":" allocates only as much space as you tell it to","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"(padded to a round value), and no more. This avoids over-allocation, but","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"can result in insertion not having amortized constant-time performance.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The following code declares "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"values"},{"type":"text","text":", an array of integers, and the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"addTenQuadratic()"},{"type":"text","text":" function, which adds ten more values to the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"values"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"array on each call."}]},{"code":["  var values: [Int] = [0, 1, 2, 3]","","  \/\/ Don't use 'reserveCapacity(_:)' like this","  func addTenQuadratic() {","      let newCount = values.count + 10","      values.reserveCapacity(newCount)","      for n in values.count..<newCount {","          values.append(n)","      }","  }"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The call to "},{"code":"reserveCapacity(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" increases the "},{"code":"values","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" array’s capacity"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"by exactly 10 elements on each pass through "},{"code":"addTenQuadratic()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", which"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is linear growth. Instead of having constant time when averaged over"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"many calls, the function may decay to performance that is linear in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"values.count","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". This is almost certainly not what you want."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In cases like this, the simplest fix is often to simply remove the call"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to "},{"code":"reserveCapacity(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and let the "},{"code":"append(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" method grow the array"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"for you."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["  func addTen() {","      let newCount = values.count + 10","      for n in values.count..<newCount {","          values.append(n)","      }","  }"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If you need more control over the capacity of your array, implement your"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"own geometric growth strategy, passing the size you compute to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"reserveCapacity(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"O("},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}]},{"type":"text","text":"), where "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}]},{"type":"text","text":" is the number of elements in the array."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"aside","style":"note","name":"Complexity"}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Array\/reserveCapacity(_:)","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Adding-Elements","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Array\/append(_:)","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Array\/insert(_:at:)","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Array\/insert(contentsOf:at:)","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Array\/replaceSubrange(_:with:)","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Array\/replaceSubrange(_:with:)-7293p"],"title":"Adding Elements"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Reserves enough space to store the specified number of elements."}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swift\/array\/reservecapacity(_:)"]}],"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Instance Method","modules":[{"name":"Swift"}],"platforms":[{"deprecated":false,"introducedAt":"8.0","beta":false,"name":"iOS","unavailable":false},{"deprecated":false,"introducedAt":"8.0","beta":false,"name":"iPadOS","unavailable":false},{"deprecated":false,"introducedAt":"13.0","beta":false,"name":"Mac Catalyst","unavailable":false},{"unavailable":false,"introducedAt":"10.10","name":"macOS